            <ArticleTitle>Diffuse pain syndromes in the elderly.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>673-82</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Diffuse pain syndromes are common in older persons. Fibromyalgia and PMR are the most common but other inflammatory, endocrine and neoplastic diseases may cause diffuse pain as well. A thorough history and physical examination, screening laboratories and response to a trial of low-dose steroids may help to differentiate between syndromes. Fibromyalgia may be a secondary phenomenon associated with some of the other diffuse pain syndromes. This should be kept in mind if a patient fails to respond appropriately to treatments directed at a particular disease.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
